  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $y=5$, we substitute $y=5$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(5-6)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =17 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+1+{z}^{2} & =17 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & ={4}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $xz$-plane gives us the equation of the circle of radius $4$ centered at $(1,0).$",
